{"items":[{"abstract_source":null,"affected_versions":[],"affiliations":[],"authors":[],"cves":["CVE-2026-119924"],"date_precision":"exact","fetched_at":"2026-11-08T02:44:19.364465Z","first_seen_at":"2026-11-08T02:44:19.364465Z","id":"osv:CVE-2026-119924","is_backfill":false,"lang":"en","products":[],"published_at":"2026-11-06T18:38:50.951000Z","published_year":null,"raw_text":null,"references":["https://aws.amazon.com/security/security-bulletins/2026-166-aws/","https://github.com/CVEProject/cvelistV5/tree/main/cves/2026/119xxx/CVE-2026-119924.json","https://github.com/babelfish-for-postgresql/babelfish-for-postgresql/releases/tag/BABEL_4_10_0__PG_16_14","https://github.com/babelfish-for-postgresql/babelfish-for-postgresql/releases/tag/BABEL_5_6_0__PG_17_10","https://github.com/babelfish-for-postgresql/babelfish-for-postgresql/releases/tag/BABEL_6_1_0__PG_18_4","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-119924"],"risk":{"cvss_score":null,"cvss_vector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N","due_date":null,"epss_percentile":null,"epss_score":null,"exploit_in_the_wild":null,"exploit_maturity":"unreported","exploit_references":[],"has_public_exploit":false,"kev_date_added":null,"kev_listed":false,"kev_status":"unknown","known_exploited":null,"known_ransomware":null,"patch_references":["https://osv.dev/vulnerability/CVE-2026-119924"],"patch_status":"available","severity":null},"source_info":{"link_kind":"article","native_id":"CVE-2026-119924","source":"osv","source_name":"OSV.dev","source_quality":"primary","source_sub":"osv.dev","source_url":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/CVE-2026-119924"},"summary":"An out-of-bounds read in the TDS RPC procedure-name parser in the Babelfish for PostgreSQL extension versions 1.0-1.5, 2.1-2.15, 3.1-3.12, 4.0-4.8, 5.1-5.4 and in Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL with Babelfish might allow remote authenticated users to read adjacent process memory or cause a denial of service via a malformed TDS RPC request to the TDS port (default 1433).\n\n\n\nTo remediate this issue, we recommend users upgrade to Babelfish for PostgreSQL extension versions 4.10, 5.6, 6.1 or later. As a workaround, restrict network access to the TDS port (default 1433). Customers using Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL with Babelfish should upgrade their cluster to Aurora PostgreSQL 13.9.16 (1.5.5), 13.23.3 (1.17.2), 14.6.16 (2.3.5), 14.17.8 (2.12.4), 14.18.6 (2.13.3), 14.19.5 (2.14.2), 14.20.5 (2.15.2), 14.22.3 (2.16.1), 14.23.1 (2.17.0), 15.10.8 (3.8.4), 15.12.8 (3.9.4), 15.13.6 (3.10.3), 15.14.5 (3.11.2), 15.15.5 (3.12.2), 15.17.3 (3.13.1), 15.18.1 (3.14.0), 16.8.8 (4.5.5), 16.9.6 (4.6.3), 16.10.5 (4.7.2), 16.11.5 (4.8.2), 16.13.3 (4.9.1), 16.14.1 (4.10.0), 17.4.8 (5.1.4), 17.5.6 (5.2.3), 17.6.5 (5.3.2), 17.7.5 (5.4.2), 17.9.3 (5.5.1), 17.10.1 (5.6.0), 18.3.4 (6.0.2), 18.4.1 (6.1.0) or later, and apply any pending maintenance to ensure they are on the latest patch.","threat_meta":null,"title":"Out-of-Bounds Read in Babelfish for PostgreSQL TDS RPC Procedure-Name Parser","topics":["advisory","cwe-125"],"type":"advisory","updated_at":"2026-11-07T10:47:28.112985Z","vendors":[]},{"abstract_source":null,"affected_versions":[],"affiliations":[],"authors":[],"cves":["CVE-2026-123357"],"date_precision":"exact","fetched_at":"2026-11-08T02:44:19.364465Z","first_seen_at":"2026-11-08T02:44:19.364465Z","id":"osv:CVE-2026-123357","is_backfill":false,"lang":"en","products":[],"published_at":"2026-11-06T18:37:43.856000Z","published_year":null,"raw_text":null,"references":["https://github.com/CVEProject/cvelistV5/tree/main/cves/2026/123xxx/CVE-2026-123357.json","https://github.com/grobidOrg/grobid/pull/1477","https://github.com/grobidOrg/grobid/releases/tag/0.9.1","https://github.com/grobidOrg/grobid/security/advisories/GHSA-mgxf-7mg7-qpmf","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-123357"],"risk":{"cvss_score":null,"cvss_vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:N","due_date":null,"epss_percentile":null,"epss_score":null,"exploit_in_the_wild":null,"exploit_maturity":"unreported","exploit_references":[],"has_public_exploit":false,"kev_date_added":null,"kev_listed":false,"kev_status":"unknown","known_exploited":null,"known_ransomware":null,"patch_references":["https://osv.dev/vulnerability/CVE-2026-123357"],"patch_status":"available","severity":null},"source_info":{"link_kind":"article","native_id":"CVE-2026-123357","source":"osv","source_name":"OSV.dev","source_quality":"primary","source_sub":"osv.dev","source_url":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/CVE-2026-123357"},"summary":"GROBID is machine learning software for extracting information from scholarly documents. Prior to 0.9.1, the Linux non-server PDF conversion path in grobid-core/src/main/java/org/grobid/core/document/DocumentSource.java passes an attacker-influenced PDF filename through DocumentSource.pdfalto, which interpolates the path into a bash -c command string. A single quote in the filename can terminate the intended quoting, and ProcessRunner.run in grobid-core/src/main/java/org/grobid/core/process/ProcessRunner.java starts the resulting command through ProcessBuilder, allowing arbitrary commands to execute with GROBID process privileges. The bundled REST server path is not affected. This issue is fixed in version 0.9.1.","threat_meta":null,"title":"GROBID is vulnerable to OS command injection through crafted PDF filenames","topics":["advisory","cwe-78"],"type":"advisory","updated_at":"2026-11-07T10:57:29.678520Z","vendors":[]},{"abstract_source":null,"affected_versions":[],"affiliations":[],"authors":[],"cves":["CVE-2026-119923"],"date_precision":"exact","fetched_at":"2026-11-08T02:44:19.364465Z","first_seen_at":"2026-11-08T02:44:19.364465Z","id":"osv:CVE-2026-119923","is_backfill":false,"lang":"en","products":[],"published_at":"2026-11-06T18:35:49.413000Z","published_year":null,"raw_text":null,"references":["https://aws.amazon.com/security/security-bulletins/2026-166-aws/","https://github.com/CVEProject/cvelistV5/tree/mai